===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:gold|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|gold}}, from {{inh|en|ang|gold|t=gold}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*golþ}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*gulþą|t=gold}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰl̥h₃tóm|t=gold}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰelh₃-|t=green, yellow}}. Related to [[yellow]]; see there for more. Germanic cognates include {{cog|sco|gowd}}, {{cog|nl|goud}}, {{cog|de|Gold}}, {{cog|fo,is,nb,nn|gull}}, {{cog|da,sv|guld}}, and cognates from other Indo-European languages include {{cog|lv|zelts}}, {{cog|ru|зо́лото}}, {{cog|fa|زرد|tr=zard||yellow, golden}}, {{cog|sa|हिरण्य}}. {{C|en|Gold}}

